# ── RAW camera originals: keep them OUT of git entirely ─────────────────────
#
# This repo is PUBLIC, so any committed raw is world-readable forever — deleting
# it in a later commit does NOT remove it from history (and raws carry EXIF GPS).
# Workflow (enabled 2026-08-07): keep unprocessed originals in the gitignored
# /raw/ folder below, and commit ONLY the processed, EXIF-stripped derivatives
# that the build serves. Process raws into web assets with:
#   node scripts/process-community-media.mjs <slug> <prefix> --from <raw dir>
# The processed files (<prefix>-01.jpg / <prefix>-video-01.mp4) never match the
# camera patterns below, so they are still committed normally.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore only stops NEW raws from being added; it does not touch the
# ~324 raw blobs already in history (they bloat .git to ~1.7 GB and stay public).
# Removing those requires a history rewrite + force-push — a separate, manual,
# destructive step for Ava to run deliberately (see HANDOVER §6).

# Camera-pattern originals anywhere under public/
public/images/**/*.[Hh][Ee][Ii][Cc]
public/images/**/*.[Hh][Ee][Ii][Ff]
public/images/**/*.[Mm][Oo][Vv]
public/images/**/*.[Tt][Ii][Ff]
public/images/**/*.[Tt][Ii][Ff][Ff]
public/images/**/IMG_*
public/images/**/DSC*
public/images/**/DCIM*
public/images/**/100_*
public/images/**/*_Original*

# Unprocessed originals live here, outside public/ and out of git.
# The README is kept so the folder's purpose is documented in the repo.
/raw/*
!/raw/README.md

# Local-only verification harnesses (Playwright; needs `npm i --no-save playwright`)
verify-*.mjs
diag.mjs

# Local-only content-editing cheatsheet (personal reference, not part of the site)
CONTENT-GUIDE.md

# Local-only handoff doc (written for someone else's project, not part of this site)
instructions.md

# Local-only application drafts (hackathons, scholarships, programmes). This
# repo is PUBLIC — these hold personal essays, financial-need statements, and
# unpublished answers. Ignore the FOLDER, not filenames: a draft then stays
# private whatever it's called. Don't go back to bare filenames like
# `hackmit.md` — unanchored, they match at any depth, and that rule silently
# swallowed the public project page at src/content/projects/hackmit.md.
/applications/

# Wrangler local cache + miniflare state (regenerated on every wrangler run)
worker/.wrangler/
